{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel were in the wilderness.</b> For it had been decreed upon them that they would not enter the land. In the commandments above, such as libations and challah, it is written about them ״כי תבאו אל הארץ״ — when you come — to teach that they apply only in the land. But Sabbath applies both in the land and outside the land, and even in the wilderness; therefore it is written about it 'in the wilderness.'" "<b>And they found a man gathering wood.</b> Rashi explained: the verse speaks in disparagement of Israel — that they kept only the first Sabbath, and on the second this one came and profaned it. It is thus found that the gatherer was in the first year. And if you ask: but in the portion of Emor, Rashi explained that the gatherer and the blasphemer were in the same chapter, and regarding the blasphemer it is implied that it was in the second year, when the banners were established — one may answer: the blasphemer too was in the first year, and even so he was liable, as he explained in the portion of Emor." "<b>Gathering wood on the Sabbath day.</b> One said: he was carrying four cubits in the public domain. And one said: he was uprooting. And one said: he was making a stack — in the chapter of הזורק." "<b>And they found.</b> This teaches that Moses appointed guards over him, and they found him gathering."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:10.079010755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}